HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Python, configuration files, build scripts,
workflow definitions, and documentation — is proprietary.

No permission is granted to copy, modify, reproduce, distribute,
publish, sublicense, sell, or otherwise use the source code, in
whole or in part, without prior written permission from the
copyright holder.


----------------------------------------------------------------
2. REFERENCE DOCUMENTS
----------------------------------------------------------------

The reference documents contained in the `pdf/` directory are
administrative and academic materials. Their copyright status
varies:

  - Some are official government publications and may be in the
    public domain.
  - Some are academic or institutional publications whose rights
    belong to their original authors or publishers.
  - Some are third-party materials whose rights belong to their
    respective copyright holders.

These documents are provided for viewing and educational reference
only. No ownership is claimed over them. Redistribution, commercial
use, or modification of these documents must comply with the
original rights holders' terms.

If you are a rights holder and believe a document has been
included improperly, please contact us for prompt removal.


